          "quote": "Asleep itself never comes before a noun ... Asleep is used only after a verb",
          "severity": "blocking",
          "family": "other",
          "reason": "The entry repeatedly gives an overabsolute account of position; asleep is normally predicative but can occur postpositively after a noun, for example “the baby asleep in bed.”"
